$$SYNTAX-LEVEL 2
*(mgdb-nomenclature
<main class="mgdb-page mgdb-hub-page mgdb-nomenclature-page" id="nomenclature-main">
  <nav class="mgdb-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span><a href="/community">Community</a><span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span><span aria-current="page">Nomenclature</span>
  </nav>

  <section class="mgdb-hero nomenclature-hero" aria-labelledby="nomenclature-title">
    <div class="mgdb-hero-emblem nomenclature-hero-emblem">
      <div class="nomenclature-symbol-stack" aria-hidden="true"><span><i>dek12</i></span><span><i>Dek12</i></span><span>ADH1</span><span>Zm00001d459384</span></div>
      <strong>Maize naming standards</strong>
      <span>Genes to genomes</span>
    </div>
    <div class="mgdb-hero-body">
      <h1 id="nomenclature-title">Name maize biology clearly.</h1>
      <p class="mgdb-hero-description">Consistent names connect discoveries across experiments, publications, databases, and generations of researchers. Use the community standard for genes, alleles, gene products, markers, rearrangements, genome assemblies, annotations, and gene models &#8212; MaizeGDB is the nomenclature clearing house.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="mgdb-message mgdb-message-info nomenclature-guidance" role="note">
    <div><strong>Check first, name once.</strong> Search MaizeGDB before proposing a gene or allele name. Existing names and symbols should be retained; aliases and cross-references preserve continuity without fragmenting the scientific record.</div>
  </div>

  <nav class="mgdb-section-tabs" aria-label="Sections on this page">
    <a href="#quick-conventions" class="is-current" aria-current="true">Conventions</a>
    <a href="#choose-guidance">Guidance</a>
    <a href="#assembly-standard">Assemblies and gene models</a>
    <a href="#nomenclature-help">Before naming</a>
    <a href="#complete-standard">The standard</a>
    <a href="#nomenclature-related">Related resources</a>
  </nav>

  <section id="quick-conventions" aria-labelledby="quick-conventions-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="quick-conventions-title">Conventions</h2></div>
      <p>Formatting carries biological meaning. Use the complete standard below for edge cases, historical conventions, and formal guidance.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="nomenclature-convention-grid">
      <article class="nomenclature-convention-card">
        <span class="nomenclature-example"><i>dek12</i></span>
        <h3>Gene locus</h3>
        <p>Gene names and locus symbols are generally lower-case and italicized. A numerical suffix follows the symbol without a hyphen.</p>
        <a href="#STANDARD">Standard symbols <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="nomenclature-convention-card nomenclature-tone-green">
        <span class="nomenclature-example"><i>Dek12</i></span>
        <h3>Dominant or nonmutant allele</h3>
        <p>Allele capitalization communicates inheritance or phenotype. A hyphen introduces the designation for a particular allele.</p>
        <a href="#ALLELIC">Allelic designations <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="nomenclature-convention-card nomenclature-tone-gold">
        <span class="nomenclature-example">ADH1</span>
        <h3>Gene product</h3>
        <p>Gene-product symbols use uppercase, nonitalic type. Product names themselves are neither capitalized nor italicized.</p>
        <a href="#ALLELIC">Gene-product guidance <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="nomenclature-convention-card nomenclature-tone-red">
        <span class="nomenclature-example nomenclature-example-long">Zm00001d459384</span>
        <h3>Gene model</h3>
        <p>Gene-model identifiers combine the species code, assembly-version code, and a stable numeric identifier without encoding location.</p>
        <a href="#GENEMODEL">Gene-model identifiers <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="choose-guidance" class="nomenclature-route-section" aria-labelledby="choose-guidance-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="choose-guidance-title">Guidance</h2></div>
      <p>Jump directly to the relevant part of the complete community standard.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="nomenclature-route-grid">
      <article><h3>Genes and loci</h3><p>Definitions, anonymous transcripts, standard symbols, and related loci.</p><div><a href="#DEFINITIONS">Definitions</a><a href="#ANONYMOUS">Anonymous transcripts</a><a href="#LOCI">Related loci</a></div></article>
      <article><h3>Alleles and mutations</h3><p>Independent origins, nonmutant alleles, deletions, and transposable-element insertions.</p><div><a href="#ALLELIC">Alleles</a><a href="#DELETIONS">Deletions</a><a href="#TRANSPOSABLE">Insertions</a></div></article>
      <article><h3>Markers and chromosomes</h3><p>RFLP and RAPD names, probe acronyms, chromosome rearrangements, and organellar genes.</p><div><a href="#RFLP">RFLP and RAPD</a><a href="#CHROMOSOME">Rearrangements</a><a href="#RFLP_ACRONYMS">Acronyms</a></div></article>
      <article><h3>Gene families and products</h3><p>Transcription-factor products, gene synonyms, and cross-species prefixes.</p><div><a href="#TF">Transcription factors</a><a href="#ORGANELLAR">Organellar genes</a></div></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="assembly-standard" class="nomenclature-assembly-section" aria-labelledby="assembly-standard-title">
    <div class="nomenclature-assembly-visual" aria-hidden="true">
      <span>Zm</span><strong>ZZ99</strong><span>XGROUP</span><strong>1.0</strong>
    </div>
    <div class="nomenclature-assembly-copy">
      <h2 id="assembly-standard-title">Assemblies and gene models</h2>
      <p>Modern maize genomics requires identifiers that scale across many lines and releases. Assembly names capture species, cultivar, project, and version; compact assembly codes connect each genome to its annotations and gene models.</p>
      <div class="nomenclature-assembly-actions">
        <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-primary" href="https://documents.maizegdb.org/nomenclature/maize_assembly_nomenclature_2021.pdf">2021 nomenclature document</a>
        <a href="https://documents.maizegdb.org/nomenclature/maize_assembly_nomenclature_2016_update.pdf">2016 gene-model description <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
        <a href="#GENEMODEL">Read section 12 <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="nomenclature-primer" class="nomenclature-primer" aria-labelledby="nomenclature-primer-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="nomenclature-primer-title">How to read genome and annotation identifiers</h2></div>
      <p>Each layer adds context: a descriptive assembly name, a compact assembly code, then an annotation and gene-model suffix. The examples below are selectable HTML and reflow for small screens.</p>
    </div>

    <article class="nomenclature-id-card" aria-labelledby="assembly-name-heading">
      <div class="nomenclature-id-copy">
        <span class="nomenclature-id-step" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <div><h3 id="assembly-name-heading">Genome assembly name</h3><p>The public name identifies the maize species, sequenced cultivar or accession, the project responsible for the assembly, and its version. A change to the exact sequenced cultivar or to the sequencing group receives a new genome identifier.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="nomenclature-id-diagram" aria-label="Genome assembly name: Zm-ZZ99-XGROUP-1.0">
        <div class="nomenclature-id-parts nomenclature-id-parts-name">
          <div class="nomenclature-id-part nomenclature-part-blue"><span>Species</span><code>Zm</code></div>
          <span class="nomenclature-id-separator" aria-hidden="true">&ndash;</span>
          <div class="nomenclature-id-part nomenclature-part-green"><span>Cultivar</span><code>ZZ99</code></div>
          <span class="nomenclature-id-separator" aria-hidden="true">&ndash;</span>
          <div class="nomenclature-id-part nomenclature-part-orange"><span>Sequencing group</span><code>XGROUP</code></div>
          <span class="nomenclature-id-separator" aria-hidden="true">&ndash;</span>
          <div class="nomenclature-id-part nomenclature-part-purple"><span>Version</span><code>1.0</code></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="nomenclature-id-note"><strong>Pattern:</strong> <code>&lt;species ID&gt;-&lt;cultivar&gt;-&lt;project&gt;-&lt;assembly version&gt;.&lt;sub-version&gt;</code></p>
    </article>

    <article class="nomenclature-id-card" aria-labelledby="assembly-code-heading">
      <div class="nomenclature-id-copy">
        <span class="nomenclature-id-step" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <div><h3 id="assembly-code-heading">Genome assembly code</h3><p>The short code is a stable synonym for the assembly name and is assigned by MaizeGDB. The five-digit genome number identifies one genome; the version letter advances with every major or minor assembly update: <strong>a</strong> is the first version, <strong>b</strong> the next, and so on.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="nomenclature-id-diagram" aria-label="Genome assembly code: Zm00001e">
        <div class="nomenclature-id-parts nomenclature-id-parts-code">
          <div class="nomenclature-id-part nomenclature-part-blue"><span>Species ID</span><code>Zm</code></div>
          <div class="nomenclature-id-part nomenclature-part-green"><span>Genome number</span><code>00001</code></div>
          <div class="nomenclature-id-part nomenclature-part-orange"><span>Version letter</span><code>e</code></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="nomenclature-id-note"><strong>Pattern:</strong> <code>&lt;species ID&gt;&lt;five-digit genome number&gt;&lt;assembly version letter&gt;</code></p>
    </article>

    <article class="nomenclature-id-card" aria-labelledby="gene-model-heading">
      <div class="nomenclature-id-copy">
        <span class="nomenclature-id-step" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
        <div><h3 id="gene-model-heading">Gene model and transcript identifiers</h3><p>A representative gene model starts with its assembly code, adds the annotation major-version letter, and ends in a six-digit model suffix. A transcript appends <strong>_T</strong> and a three-digit isoform number; a protein uses <strong>_P</strong> instead.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="nomenclature-id-diagram" aria-label="Transcript identifier: Zm00001ea036589_T001">
        <div class="nomenclature-id-parts nomenclature-id-parts-gene">
          <div class="nomenclature-id-part nomenclature-part-blue"><span>Species ID</span><code>Zm</code></div>
          <div class="nomenclature-id-part nomenclature-part-red"><span>Genome / cultivar ID</span><code>00001</code></div>
          <div class="nomenclature-id-part nomenclature-part-green"><span>Assembly version</span><code>e</code></div>
          <div class="nomenclature-id-part nomenclature-part-orange"><span>Annotation version</span><code>a</code></div>
          <div class="nomenclature-id-part nomenclature-part-purple"><span>Gene-model suffix</span><code>036589</code></div>
          <div class="nomenclature-id-part nomenclature-part-cyan"><span>Transcript number</span><code>_T001</code></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="nomenclature-id-details">
        <p><strong>Annotation set:</strong> <code>Zm00001ea.1</code> means the first major annotation of assembly <code>Zm00001e</code>, first minor release. A new major annotation changes the letter; a minor release changes the number after the period while retained models keep their IDs.</p>
        <p><strong>Model behavior:</strong> the six-digit suffix is unique within the assembly and allows gaps for later additions or splits. Transcript and protein numbers are not conserved across gene-model-set versions.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="nomenclature-id-note"><strong>Patterns:</strong> gene model <code>Zm00001ea036589</code>; transcript <code>Zm00001ea036589_T001</code>; protein <code>Zm00001ea036589_P001</code></p>
    </article>

    <div class="mgdb-message mgdb-message-info nomenclature-id-takeaway" role="note">
      <div><strong>Read identifiers as provenance, not phenotype.</strong> They tell you which assembly and annotation produced a model. Coding status, function, and other biological interpretation belong in metadata rather than in the identifier itself.</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="nomenclature-help" class="nomenclature-help-section" aria-labelledby="nomenclature-help-title">
    <div>
      <h2 id="nomenclature-help-title">Before naming</h2>
      <p>Search for existing genes, symbols, aliases, and alleles. If a proposed designation is not represented, contact MaizeGDB so the nomenclature committee can help avoid duplicate or conflicting names.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="nomenclature-help-actions"><a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-primary" href="/gene_center/gene">Search genes</a><a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary" href="/contact">Contact MaizeGDB</a></div>
  </section>

  <section id="complete-standard" class="nomenclature-full-section" aria-labelledby="complete-standard-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="complete-standard-title">The standard</h2></div>
    </div>
    <p class="nomenclature-section-lead">Originally published in Maize Genetics Cooperation Newsletter 69, pages 182&ndash;184, with subsequent updates through the assembly and gene-model guidance. The text below is the curator-maintained standard itself, nested unchanged.</p>
    <div class="nomenclature-standard-content">*(full-standard)</div>
  </section>
  <section id="nomenclature-related" class="mgdb-hub-related" aria-labelledby="nomenclature-related-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div>
        <h2 id="nomenclature-related-title">Related resources</h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-resource-panel">
      <div class="mgdb-resource-list">
        <a href="/gene_center/gene">
          <strong>Gene Data Hub</strong>
          <span>Check whether a symbol, name or gene model already exists</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/data_center/locus">
          <strong>Locus Data Hub</strong>
          <span>Classic loci and the alleles named against them</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/genome">
          <strong>Genome Data Hub</strong>
          <span>The assemblies and annotations these identifiers version</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/contact">
          <strong>Contact MaizeGDB</strong>
          <span>Reach the nomenclature clearing house before assigning a name</span>
        </a>
        <a href="https://documents.maizegdb.org/nomenclature/maize_assembly_nomenclature_2021.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <strong>Assembly nomenclature, 2021</strong>
          <span>The whole-genome assembly and annotation naming document</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
)
